// BEQ unit test for Lab 9.
// inst_rom.v byte-swaps each loaded word, so these are byte-reversed
// versions of the normal 32-bit MIPS machine instructions.
//
// The program builds the serial MMIO base address in $s4, verifies one
// taken BEQ and one not-taken BEQ, prints "P" on the taken path, then
// loops forever.
@00000000
00400a20
22a00a00
22a08a02
22a08a02
22a08a02
05000820
05000920
02000911
46000a20
0c008aae
50000a20
0c008aae
07000a20
03000820
05000920
01000911
64000b20
2a001020
ffff0010
00000000
